<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Scope is deliberately minimal — Google Play requires apps to use the narrowest
    accessibility capabilities that still achieve the functionality:

    - typeWindowStateChanged only. The service discards every other event type
      (see AppBlockerAccessibilityService.onAccessibilityEvent), so subscribing to
      typeWindowContentChanged would deliver a high volume of screen-content events
      we never look at.
    - canRetrieveWindowContent is deliberately NOT declared. The service needs one
      thing — the foreground package name — and AccessibilityEvent.getPackageName()
      supplies it for typeWindowStateChanged without any content-retrieval capability.
      Declaring it would grant the ability to read window content the app never reads,
      and would make Android tell the user this service "can retrieve window content"
      while our own disclosure promises the opposite. Do not re-add it: without it the
      OS cannot hand us screen content at all, which is precisely the guarantee the
      disclosure makes.
    - isAccessibilityTool is deliberately NOT declared at all (it defaults to false).
      Spike AI is not an assistive tool for users with disabilities, so it does not
      claim to be one, and it therefore relies on in-app prominent disclosure + consent
      to satisfy Play's User Data policy. Do not add this attribute in either form:
      declaring it true would be a false claim, and declaring it false invites the
      reading that the value was considered optional rather than settled.

    The consent itself is enforced in code, not here: AppBlockerAccessibilityService
    reads nothing until AccessibilityConsent.isGranted() is true, so enabling this
    service from Android Settings without passing through the in-app disclosure grants
    no data access.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description"
    android:notificationTimeout="100" />
